  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with PCA n2000 (config_001) achieves 48.5% accuracy, while image-only with ResNet50 (config_010) is very weak at 20.8%, indicating RNA is the dominant signal. The key uncertainty is whether the linear PCA representation is capturing all useful structure or whether a learned nonlinear encoder (scvi_n200) could extract richer features. This experiment (config_004) tests scvi_n200 as a single-variable change from config_001, isolating the effect of the RNA encoder while keeping singleprofile and no aggregation constant. This is the best next step because the representation quality is the most fundamental design choice: if scvi outperforms PCA, it opens a promising path toward multiprofile+scvi and multimodal+scvi configurations; if it does not, we confirm PCA is sufficient and can redirect remaining budget toward aggregation or multimodal fusion strategies."
